CAT = "phinsContract"; SEG = "CON"
Q = [
("Under the Insurance Code, a contract of insurance is an agreement to indemnify another against loss from:",
 "An unknown or contingent event", ["A known and certain event", "Any deliberate act of the insured", "A debt that is already overdue"],
 "Section 2 defines insurance as an agreement, for a consideration, to indemnify another against loss, damage or liability arising from an unknown or contingent event."),
("Who may be insured under the Insurance Code?",
 "Anyone except a public enemy", ["Only Filipino citizens of age", "Only persons with a steady job", "Only residents of the country"],
 "Section 7 says anyone except a public enemy may be insured. A public enemy is a citizen of a country at war with the Philippines."),
("Marites, who is married, buys a policy on her own life. Her husband's consent is:",
 "Not necessary", ["Required in writing", "Required if he is named", "Required by the insurer"],
 "Section 3 states that the consent of the spouse is not necessary for a married person's policy on his or her own life or that of his or her children."),
("Section 4 of the Insurance Code says insurance cannot be taken out on:",
 "The drawing of a lottery", ["A parent's life", "A business partner's life", "A house under mortgage"],
 "Insurance for or against the drawing of a lottery, or a lottery ticket winning a prize, is not authorized. It would be gambling, not risk transfer."),
("A person has an insurable interest in the life of:",
 "His own spouse", ["A famous athlete", "A stranger next door", "A former classmate"],
 "Section 10(a) gives every person an insurable interest in the life and health of himself, his spouse and his children."),
("A lender has an insurable interest in a borrower's life because:",
 "The death may stop repayment", ["The lender likes the borrower", "The loan is secured by land", "The borrower is a relative"],
 "Section 10(c) covers any person under a legal obligation to pay money to the insured, whose death might delay or prevent payment."),
("A college student is supported by her aunt. The student has an insurable interest in:",
 "Her aunt's life", ["Her classmates' lives", "Her teacher's life", "Her landlord's life"],
 "Section 10(b) gives an insurable interest in the life of any person on whom one depends wholly or partly for education or support."),
("For life insurance on another person, insurable interest must exist:",
 "When the insurance takes effect", ["Only when the insured person dies", "At every premium due date", "Only when the policy is reinstated"],
 "Section 19 says an interest in the life or health of a person must exist when the insurance takes effect, but need not exist afterwards or at death."),
("Jojo insures his business partner's life. The partnership later ends. The policy is:",
 "Still valid", ["Void at once", "Voidable by the insurer", "Converted to term"],
 "Insurable interest in a life need only exist when the policy takes effect (Section 19), so a later end to the relationship does not void it."),
("A policy on a stranger's life taken out only to profit from the death is void because it is:",
 "A wagering contract", ["An aleatory contract", "A personal contract", "A unilateral contract"],
 "Without insurable interest the policy is a wager on a life. Section 25 makes every policy executed by way of gaming or wagering void."),
("Under the Insurance Code, concealment is:",
 "Failing to disclose a known fact", ["A false statement in writing", "A breach of a promised act", "Refusing to pay a premium on time"],
 "Section 26 defines concealment as neglect to communicate that which a party knows and ought to communicate."),
("An applicant honestly forgets to mention a past hospital stay that was material. The insurer may:",
 "Rescind the contract", ["Only raise the premium", "Do nothing at all", "Fine the applicant"],
 "Section 27 provides that concealment, whether intentional or unintentional, entitles the injured party to rescind the contract."),
("Materiality of a concealed fact is judged by:",
 "Its effect on the insurer", ["Whether it caused the death", "The size of the policy", "The insured's own opinion"],
 "Section 31 says materiality depends on the probable and reasonable influence of the facts on the other party in forming its estimate of the risk, not on the event."),
("Rey hid a heart condition when he applied and died months later in a road crash. Under Section 31, the hidden condition is:",
 "Still material to the risk", ["Immaterial, as it was unrelated", "Material only if it was fatal", "Excused by the accident"],
 "Materiality is determined not by the event but by its influence on the insurer when it accepted the risk, so an unrelated cause of death does not cure concealment."),
("An applicant need not volunteer a fact that:",
 "The insurer already knows", ["Is about his own health", "Shows a higher level of risk", "Concerns a past illness of his"],
 "Section 30 lists matters a party need not communicate unless asked, including those the other party already knows or ought to know."),
("Under Section 35, even when asked, an applicant never has to disclose:",
 "His own judgment on it", ["His medical history", "His occupation and income", "Other policies he holds"],
 "Section 35 says neither party is bound to communicate, even upon inquiry, information of his own judgment upon the matters in question. Facts about health, work and other cover must be disclosed when asked."),
("A representation in insurance may be:",
 "Oral or written", ["Written only", "Notarized only", "Sworn before a lawyer"],
 "Section 36 provides that a representation may be oral or written, and Section 37 that it may be made at or before issuance of the policy."),
("A representation may be withdrawn or changed:",
 "Before the insurance takes effect", ["At any time after the policy issues", "Only within the grace period", "Only with a court's approval"],
 "Section 41 allows a representation to be altered or withdrawn before the insurance is effected, but not afterwards."),
("If a representation is false in a material point, the injured party may:",
 "Rescind the contract", ["Collect a penalty fee", "Reduce the face amount", "Ignore it entirely"],
 "Section 45 entitles the injured party to rescind from the time the representation becomes false."),
("A statement in the policy itself about the insured, made as a fact, is:",
 "An express warranty", ["A representation", "An implied warranty", "A concealment"],
 "Section 71 makes a statement in a policy, of a matter relating to the person or risk as fact, an express warranty."),
("Every express warranty must be:",
 "In the policy or a cited paper", ["Spoken before two witnesses", "Filed with a court of law", "Approved in writing by the agent"],
 "Section 70 requires an express warranty to be contained in the policy itself or in another signed instrument referred to in the policy."),
("A breach of warranty without fraud:",
 "Exonerates the insurer from then", ["Makes the policy void ab initio", "Has no effect on the cover at all", "Forfeits every premium paid so far"],
 "Section 76 says a breach without fraud merely exonerates the insurer from the time it occurs, or prevents attachment if broken at the start."),
("The written instrument that sets out a contract of insurance is the:",
 "Policy", ["Application", "Rider", "Receipt"],
 "Section 49 calls the written instrument in which a contract of insurance is set forth a policy of insurance."),
("A rider pasted to a policy binds the insured only if:",
 "Its title is written in the policy", ["The agent initials it on the back", "It is printed in red ink", "It is mailed to the owner separately"],
 "Section 50 says an attached rider is not binding unless its descriptive title or name is also written on the blank spaces of the policy."),
("A rider issued after the policy, not applied for by the owner, takes effect when:",
 "The owner countersigns it", ["The agent hands it over", "The insurer stamps it as received", "Thirty days have passed"],
 "Under Section 50, such a rider must be countersigned by the insured or owner, which shows agreement to its contents."),
("May a life policy be issued in electronic form?",
 "Yes, under the E-Commerce Act", ["No, a paper policy is required", "Only for group life policies", "Only if a notary signs it"],
 "Section 50 allows electronic policies subject to Republic Act No. 8792, the Electronic Commerce Act, and the Commissioner's rules."),
("As a rule, an insurance policy is not valid and binding until:",
 "The premium is paid", ["The agent signs it", "The insured reads it", "A claim is filed"],
 "Section 77 says no policy is valid and binding unless and until the premium is paid, with exceptions such as the life grace period."),
("Which is an exception to the rule that premium must be paid before cover binds?",
 "The life grace period", ["A verbal promise to pay", "A post-dated check alone", "The agent's own guarantee"],
 "Section 77 excepts a life or industrial life policy while the grace period applies, and a credit extension under licensed intermediary agreements."),
("A policy acknowledges receipt of the premium. Under Section 79, this is:",
 "Conclusive proof of payment", ["Evidence the court may reject", "Valid only with a receipt", "Binding on the insured only"],
 "An acknowledgment of premium in the policy is conclusive evidence of payment so far as to make the policy binding."),
("A government employee wants premiums deducted from her salary. The Insurance Code:",
 "Allows salary deduction", ["Forbids salary deduction", "Requires a court order", "Allows it for non-life only"],
 "Section 78 lets employees of the government and of GOCCs pay insurance premiums and loan obligations through salary deduction."),
("An insured who annulled a policy because of the insurer's misrepresentation may get:",
 "A return of the premium", ["Double the face amount", "Nothing back at all", "Only the agent's commission"],
 "Section 82 entitles the insured to a return of premium when the contract is annulled because of the fraud or misrepresentation of the insurer or its agent."),
("If a claim is denied because of the insured's fraud, the premiums are:",
 "Not returned", ["Returned in full", "Returned with interest", "Paid to the beneficiary"],
 "Section 82 states that the insured is not entitled to a return of premium if the policy is annulled, rescinded or the claim denied by reason of fraud."),
]
